---
/**
 * @file terms.astro
 * @description Terms of Use page detailing independent project status and disclaimer.
 */

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
	title="Terms of Use & Legal Disclaimers | mapaPH" 
	description="Read the complete Terms of Use for mapaPH. Learn about open-source MIT licensing, public-domain Philippine government datasets, geodetic survey disclaimers under RA 8560, and transit tariff terms."
>
	<script type="application/ld+json" slot="schema" is:inline>
		{
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@graph": [
				{
					"@type": "WebPage",
					"name": "Terms of Use | mapaPH",
					"url": "https://www.mapaph.com/terms",
					"description": "Terms of Use, open-source MIT licensing, public-domain government data attribution, and engineering/transit disclaimers for mapaPH."
				},
				{
					"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
					"itemListElement": [
						{
							"@type": "ListItem",
							"position": 1,
							"name": "Home",
							"item": "https://www.mapaph.com"
						},
						{
							"@type": "ListItem",
							"position": 2,
							"name": "Terms of Use",
							"item": "https://www.mapaph.com/terms"
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
	</script>

	<Navbar />

	<main id="main-content" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 text-mapa-ink">
		<article>
			<span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-green">
				Legal & Licensing
			</span>
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-mapa-green tracking-tight sm:text-5xl font-serif mt-2">
				Terms of Use
			</h1>
			
			<p class="font-sans text-xs text-mapa-muted mt-2">
				Last updated: October 2026
			</p>

			<div class="mt-10 border-t border-mapa-contour/60 pt-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4">
					1. Acceptance of Terms
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					By accessing and browsing the mapaPH hub (<a href="https://www.mapaph.com" class="text-mapa-green hover:underline">www.mapaph.com</a>), using any of our interactive mapping calculators, or downloading GeoJSON boundary exports, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Use. If you do not agree to these terms, please discontinue use of the site.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					2. Description of the Service
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					mapaPH is an independent, open-source civic cartography hub and technical documentation portal that builds browser-native utilities around maps and spatial datasets of the Philippines. Our suite includes administrative code decoders (PSGC and PHLPost ZIP directories), geodetic coordinate converters (PRS92 and WGS84), public transit and expressway tariff estimators, highway milestone locators, and the Lens choropleth visualizer.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					3. Non-Government Independence Disclaimer
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					mapaPH is an independent civic technology project developed and maintained by private open-source contributors. We are <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or acting on behalf of any government agency, municipal authority, or public corporation of the Republic of the Philippines</strong>, including the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA), National Mapping and Resource Information Authority (NAMRIA), Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board (LTFRB), Toll Regulatory Board (TRB), Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH), Department of Transportation (DOTr), Philippine Postal Corporation (PHLPost), or Commission on Elections (COMELEC).
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					4. Intellectual Property, MIT License, and Public Domain Data
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Resources hosted on mapaPH fall into three distinct legal categories:
				</p>

				<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark font-sans">
					<table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
						<thead class="border-b border-mapa-contour bg-mapa-canvas text-mapa-ink uppercase text-[11px] font-bold">
							<tr>
								<th class="p-3">Asset Category</th>
								<th class="p-3">Governing License / Statute</th>
								<th class="p-3">Permitted Use</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody class="divide-y divide-mapa-contour/50 text-mapa-ink/85">
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3 font-semibold text-mapa-green">Application Source Code & Scripts</td>
								<td class="p-3">MIT Open-Source License</td>
								<td class="p-3">Free to inspect, fork, modify, and redistribute for commercial or non-commercial use with copyright notice preserved.</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3 font-semibold text-mapa-navy">Government Statistical & Tariff Data</td>
								<td class="p-3">RA 8293 Sec. 176 &amp; EO No. 2 (s. 2016)</td>
								<td class="p-3">Works of the Government of the Philippines are in the public domain. Users should cite the originating agency (PSA, NAMRIA, LTFRB, TRB, PHLPost).</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td class="p-3 font-semibold text-mapa-rust">Basemap Tiles &amp; OCHA Boundaries</td>
								<td class="p-3">ODbL 1.0 / CC BY 4.0</td>
								<td class="p-3">OpenStreetMap tiles require attribution to OpenStreetMap contributors; UN OCHA HDX boundaries require attribution to NAMRIA/PSA/HDX.</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					5. Geodetic & Cadastral Surveying Disclaimer (RA 8560)
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Under <strong>Republic Act No. 8560 (The Philippine Geodetic Engineering Act of 1998)</strong> and DENR Administrative Order No. 2007-29, only a duly registered and licensed Geodetic Engineer is legally authorized to execute relocation surveys, subdivision plans, and cadastral boundary verifications for land titling in the Philippines. The PRS92 to WGS84 coordinate transformations, Transverse Mercator calculations, and simplified GeoJSON municipal polygons provided on mapaPH are intended strictly for GIS visualization, academic research, and preliminary spatial planning. They must never be used to adjudicate property boundary disputes, establish legal lot monuments, or substitute for an official survey plan approved by the DENR Land Management Bureau (LMB) or Land Registration Authority (LRA).
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					6. Public Transit, Rail, and Expressway Tariff Disclaimer
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Our Commute Fare Estimator, Metro Manila Rail Transit Guide, EDSA Carousel Calculator, and Expressway Toll Calculator compute fares based on published LTFRB Board Resolutions, DOTr Department Orders, LRTA tariff tables, and TRB toll matrices. However, fuel subsidy adjustments, provisional tariff petitions, toll plaza reclassifications, and route diversions can occur between dataset updates. In all commercial transit and tollway transactions, the official laminated <strong>LTFRB Fare Matrix (<em>Talaan ng Pamasahe</em>)</strong> displayed inside the vehicle or the electronic toll deduction recorded at the concessionaire's barrier gantry (Autosweep / Easytrip) governs the legally binding fare.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					7. Warranty Disclaimer and Limitation of Liability
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					All tools, services, maps, and geographic datasets on mapaPH are provided strictly on an "as-is" and "as-available" basis, without warranties of any kind, either express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the project maintainers and contributors shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages resulting from the use of or inability to use our tools, including transit delays, toll balance penalties, routing discrepancies, or spatial projection errors.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					8. User Conduct and Prohibited Uses
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					You agree to use our tools only for lawful civic, educational, personal, or professional purposes. You are prohibited from:
				</p>
				<ul class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 list-disc pl-5 mb-6 space-y-2">
					<li>
						Launching automated denial-of-service attacks or abusive scraping traffic that degrades CDN availability for other users (if you need raw JSON datasets, please download them directly from our public GitHub repository instead of scraping HTML pages).
					</li>
					<li>
						Misrepresenting mapaPH visualizations or exports as official government-issued certificates or certified cadastral plans.
					</li>
					<li>
						Using our tools for real-time safety-critical navigation, aviation, maritime piloting, or emergency dispatch where approximation tolerances could lead to physical harm.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink font-serif mb-4 mt-10">
					9. Governing Law, Jurisdiction, and Contact
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					These Terms of Use are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of the Philippines. Any legal disputes arising out of these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the appropriate courts of the Philippines. For questions regarding licensing, terms, or attribution, please contact us at <a href="mailto:vrsmagwili@gmail.com" class="text-mapa-green underline font-medium">vrsmagwili@gmail.com</a> or visit our <a href="/contact" class="text-mapa-green underline font-medium">Contact Page</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</BaseLayout>
